    "summary": "Fish-hook, of  native (?) copper, of rectangular cross section, with a drop shaped bone or antler sinker, flat on one side and slightly domed on the other. The hook is bent, set into the sinker and passed through a hole in the sinker, with a flattened head on the far side. Above are two holes  for the line, countersunked on the rounded side; and to one side at the distal end is a further hole originally to hold a line to secure the bait, of which only a short section of sinew survives.",
